<title>FINLAND: CULTOR LICENCES TECHNOLOGY TO TUCHENHAGEN.</title>
<headline>CULTOR LICENCES TECHNOLOGY TO TUCHENHAGEN.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish Cultor Oy said in a statement on Tuesday it would license its immobilized yeast technology to Tuchenhagen, part of the German GEA Group.</p>
<p>Cultor decided to license the technology, used mainly for fermented beverages, to Tuchenhagen to enable itself to further concentrate on its core businesses, it said.</p>
<p>The technology had been developed by Cultor in cooperation with Finnish brewers and had been licensed to eight breweries around the world.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 248</p>
</text>
